<title>UK: INTERVIEW-Thorn sees 12 pct EPS enhancement.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-Thorn sees 12 pct EPS enhancement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rentals firm Thorn Plc said on Wednesday its plans to return 87 million stg cash to shareholders would enhance earnings per share on a pro forma basis by 12 percent over a 12 month period.</p>
<p>The company, owner of Radio Rentals in Britain and Rent-a-Center in the United States, also said it would make a 17.1 million stg provision for litigation in the U.S.</p>
<p>This represents the upper limit of damages Thorn could face in a case in Minnesota relating to its rental agreements. But Thorn said it would appeal against such an award of damages.</p>
</text>
